# Bob's gully (design section 10.1): a sand ledge at 22,63,126 boxed in by a pond and 2-high
# Spawn-protected sand; in the sandbox it was only escapable by swimming.
#
# REAL cells: x 20..24, y 60..64, z 124..128, loaded verbatim from gully/bob_ledge_22_63_126.txt by
# the `dump` line (last line, so it overrides the assumed fills). Every solid cell in it is marked
# protected (the Spawn-base zone); sandstone maps to stone (#/P). The ledge air cell (@) is NOT
# protected (assumption: the zone covers the blocks, so a 1-block dirt stair at the ledge is legal).
#
# ASSUMED cells (no dump yet), each fill below says what it stands for:
name gully_ledge
origin 14 56 116
size 21 14 20
tool HAND
start 22 63 126
goal 31 63 126
flags swim=1 break=1 place=1 scaffold=0 sprint=1
# assumed: stone under everything up to y59 (the pond floor; the real dump shows water down to y60,
# so the pond is at least 3 deep there, not the 2 the design text says)
fill 14 56 116 34 59 135 #
# assumed: the pond continues north and east of the dump, water y60..62
fill 20 60 116 28 62 127 ~
# assumed: west Spawn-base plateau, protected sand topped at y64 (stand at y65)
fill 14 60 116 19 64 135 p
# assumed: the dump's z128 stone ridge continues south and east, protected, topped at y64
fill 20 60 128 28 64 135 P
# assumed: east terrace beyond the pond, unprotected stone topped at y62 (stand at y63); the goal
fill 29 60 116 34 62 135 #
# real: the dump (overrides the fills above inside x20..24, z124..128)
dump gully/bob_ledge_22_63_126.txt 22 63 126 protect
